        {
            "number": 6,
            "revision": "753539a5ff0bab69dbdb3d9ddc2ac97255bb0a23",
            "parents": [
                "d1e720fb15ff3459f667f343b88a3fcee111d90f"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/64/83964/6",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "cchoux",
                "email": "cosmo.chou@quantatw.com",
                "username": "cchoux"
            },
            "createdOn": 1761739797,
            "author": {
                "name": "cchoux",
                "email": "cosmo.chou@quantatw.com",
                "username": "cchoux"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "How does the code know which one of these devices is being updated? Like if there's 5 of them and you're only updating the first.  Or does code update just do all of the same type at once?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "cchoux",
                        "email": "cosmo.chou@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "cchoux"
                    },
                    "message": "FirmwareName uses the \"Name\" of a firmware entry, e.g., On Yosemite5, there are 3 VR components of the same type, \"MP2X6XXFirmware\"; one of them is \"Yosemite5_MB_VR_SOC\".\n```\n{\n    \"Name\": \"Yosemite5_MB_VR_SOC\",\n    \"Type\": \"MP2X6XXFirmware\",\n    ...\n},\n{\n    \"Name\": \"Yosemite5_MB_VR_CPU0\",\n    \"Type\": \"MP2X6XXFirmware\",\n    ...\n},\n{\n    \"Name\": \"Yosemite5_MB_VR_CPU1\",\n    \"Type\": \"MP2X6XXFirmware\",\n    ...\n},\n...\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Makes sense, thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks fine to me though I see there is ongoing discussion on the dbus-sensors side of things"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 865,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "?  Really not following why we're referencing two configs here.  Shouldn't we just have the Firmware Id here?  Presumably that's lookupable from the type (ie TPS25990) without needing to encode it here?"
                },
                {
